# ============================================================================
# Unreal Engine 5 .gitignore
# Based on the canonical GitHub/Epic UnrealEngine template, plus project rules.
# NOTE: .gitignore only affects UNTRACKED files. Anything already committed
# stays tracked until explicitly `git rm --cached`.
# ============================================================================

# --- Project-specific -------------------------------------------------------

# Stale TASK-019 PIE dev-test Blueprints — throwaway helpers, not shipping
# content (TASK-039 ruling).
/Content/Dev/

# Local Claude Code permission/MCP settings — machine-specific, may accrue
# approved commands/paths. Kept out of the repo so it can't be pushed public.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Art-pipeline working dirs (TASK-084). The uv-managed virtualenv is a vendored
# site-packages tree (700+ files) — never committed; `uv sync` recreates it.
# Inbox/ holds Jonathan's concept PNGs, Cache/ holds generate/refine outputs —
# both are local working data. The .gitkeep placeholders stay tracked via the
# negations (git only honors `!` if the parent dir itself is not ignored, hence
# the `/*` form).
Tools/ArtPipeline/.venv/
Tools/ArtPipeline/Inbox/*
!Tools/ArtPipeline/Inbox/.gitkeep
Tools/ArtPipeline/Cache/*
!Tools/ArtPipeline/Cache/.gitkeep

# LLM model weights (LLM-ASSISTANT batch) — NEVER committed, in ANY form.
# `Tools/fetch_llm_model.py` downloads these on demand and the exact build is
# pinned in Plugins/SiegeLlama/Source/ThirdParty/LlamaCpp/VERSION.md, so the
# weights are a reproducible artifact, not repo content.
# ⚠️ THIS RULE IS LOAD-BEARING. A GGUF is ~2.5 GB. Git history is APPEND-ONLY,
# so a single accidental commit is permanent for every clone and can only be
# undone by rewriting history. The identical trap already fired once on this
# batch — 2026-08-02, commit 20c8e48 swept 70.7 MB of llama.cpp DLLs in as raw
# blobs and had to be repaired as e70f5ba while still unpushed. LFS is NOT the
# answer here: these weights should not be versioned at all.
*.gguf
/Models/
# ⛔ NOTHING UNDER /Models/ CAN BE RE-INCLUDED BY A `!` NEGATION — AND NOTHING
# SHOULD BE. TASK-499 (2026-08-03) STRUCK TWO DEAD RULES THAT USED TO SIT HERE,
# `!Models/.gitkeep` and `!Models/README.md`. Git does not descend into an
# ignored DIRECTORY, so it never sees a `!` for a path inside one. Verified live
# before the strike: `git check-ignore -v Models/README.md` reported the
# `/Models/` directory rule (then at line 132), and neither negated file has
# ever existed on disk or in the index — anything put in Models/ meaning to be
# tracked was being swallowed in silence.
# The directory form is used here deliberately INSTEAD of the `Models/*` +
# negation form used for Tools/ArtPipeline above. A traversable Models/ would
# open a WORKING re-include surface inside the one directory that holds the
# 2.5 GB GGUF — the carve-out CONVENTIONS "THE FINE-TUNE RUNG" §9 forbids — and
# it would buy nothing: fetch_llm_model.py creates the directory itself
# (`dest_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)`), so no .gitkeep is needed.
# ⇒ MODEL DOCUMENTATION CANNOT LIVE IN Models/. IT LIVES IN Docs/ — the shipping
#   manifest is pinned at Docs/ModelManifest.md (FINE-TUNE RUNG §5 and §9).

# ACCOUNTS Phase 2 (TASK-641, ACC-§11 config home): the REAL Supabase dev
# config — project URL + anon key + the DB-password custody comment — lives
# ONLY in this gitignored file. The committed placeholder template is
# Config/SiegeCloudDev.ini.example.
Config/SiegeCloudDev.ini

# Branch junk-strip guards (TASK-246): Python bytecode caches, FBX-import
# texture-extraction dirs (UE writes <name>.fbm/ beside the source FBX), and
# Jonathan's GDD homework PDF (kept on disk, untracked by ruling).
__pycache__/
*.fbm/
Docs/GDD-Submission-*.pdf

# --- IDE / editor -----------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
*.opensdf
*.opendb
*.sdf
*.sln
*.suo
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace

# --- Compiled binaries / libraries ------------------------------------------
*.slo
*.lo
*.o
*.obj
*.gch
*.pch
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.lai
*.la
*.a
*.lib
*.exe
*.out
*.app
*.pdb
*.mod
*.smod

# --- Unreal Engine generated directories ------------------------------------
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/

# Plugin-generated output (source/content of plugins is still tracked).
Plugins/*/Binaries/
Plugins/*/Intermediate/

# --- Unreal Engine generated assets -----------------------------------------
# Built lighting/nav data — regenerated by the editor. (This project runs
# with static lighting disabled, so these should be empty/absent anyway.)
*_BuiltData.uasset

# Source art working files (re-exported to Content/ on import).
SourceArt/**/*.png
SourceArt/**/*.tga

# --- Packaged builds --------------------------------------------------------
/Build/*
!/Build/*/
/Build/*/**
!/Build/*/PakBlacklist*.txt
!/Build/**/*.ico
/Builds/
/Packaged/

# --- OS cruft ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- SiegeLlama vendored third-party (LLM-ASSISTANT batch) ----------------
# The global *.dll / *.lib rules above would silently swallow these.
# Placed AFTER those rules on purpose: last matching pattern wins. The parent
# directories are not themselves ignored (only Plugins/*/Binaries/ and
# Plugins/*/Intermediate/ are, and the vendored tree lives under Source/), which
# is what makes these negations effective -- git will not descend into an
# ignored directory to honour a "!" inside it.
!Plugins/SiegeLlama/Source/ThirdParty/LlamaCpp/lib/**/*.lib
!Plugins/SiegeLlama/Source/ThirdParty/LlamaCpp/bin/**/*.dll
# Model weights NEVER enter git (~2.5 GB). Tools/fetch_llm_model.py fetches
# them into /Models, which is ignored wholesale.
# Restated after the negations above ON PURPOSE: last matching pattern wins, so
# the final word on the weights is an ignore and never a `!`. This duplication
# of the block near the top of the file is a backstop, not an oversight
# (TASK-499) — redundancy in the IGNORE direction is free; redundancy in the
# NEGATION direction is the incident this rule exists to prevent.
*.gguf
/Models/
